frontend: no fixed cap on YCbCr surface textures; every refused or large allocation on the console with its geometry; the device's limits

The VM's frontend refused every two-plane YCbCr surface texture over 1 Mpx (1024 x 1024 pixels), but plane 0 of a 4:2:0 one in
WindowServer, which the runtime reads in place ("surface texture refused: 4096x2160 YCbCr format 503 converts on the CPU"). That was a
rule against the memory of the runtime's conversion, not a limit of the GPU: metal2vulkan makes such a texture as an RGBA16Float image
of the converted texels (8 bytes a texel) and a staging copy of both planes, 67.5 + 25.3 = 92.8 MiB at 4096x2160 (the "about 97 MB"),
and converts on the GPU (one dispatch, skipped while the planes are unchanged). The login window's aerial wallpaper (4096x2160 frames,
format 503, YCbCr 8-bit 4:4:4 over two planes: 25.3 MiB a frame) was refused at every frame and never drawn. Now:
- No fixed cap: a surface texture is made when the runtime, Turnip and the kernel can make it; each of those refuses with its own
  reason (the runtime's error, Turnip's "NativeAdreno: a BO of N MiB is past ...", the kernel's "gpu BoAlloc refused: ...").
- Every refused surface texture (each check of the surface method: 1 plane, 2 base, 3 plane range, 4 import, 5 texture), every one
  that cost 64 MiB or more of device memory or lies over a surface of 256 MiB or more, and every YCbCr one over 1 Mpx is two lines:
  "native-metal: surface texture 4096x2160 fmt 503 YCbCr8 4:4:4 plane 0: made, 92.8M of device memory for it" (or "(at O, row R):
  refused (step): why"), then "native-metal: surface '444v' 4096x2160 25.3M, p0 4096x2160 1B r4096/4096 @0 8.4M p1 4096x2160 2B
  r8192/4096 @8847360 16.9M": the surface's four-character code, size and allocation, each plane's size, bytes per element, row bytes
  and their alignment, offset and rows x height. The device memory is the runtime's own count (nmb_device_memory_counts) across the call.
- A texture of 16 Mi texels or more says its layout bytes (the runtime's heap size), made or refused, with maxBufferLength; a refused
  buffer its length and maxBufferLength, a buffer of 256 MiB or more that it was made.
- The texture dimensions the base class left at 0 (maxTextureWidth1D, maxTextureWidth3D/Height3D/Depth3D, maxTextureDimensionCube,
  maxTextureBufferWidth) and recommendedMaxWorkingSetSize, currentAllocatedSize are answered, from this bundle's Turnip
  (tu_darwin_limits, Turnip 0008) and the runtime's memory counts; at open each process says "native-metal: limits: 2D 16384, cube
  16384, 3D 2048, layers 2048; buffer B (kernel object K, window W), heap H; IOSurface 16384x16384".
Made lines go to stderr and the unified log as NBLOG's (8 per call site, then the 16th, 32nd, ...) without a problem note.
Applied by tooling/metal/build-turnip-a830.sh after 0002. MIT, as the file.

